{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## OPERATOR-APPROVED DESIGN (2026-08-24) — settled via /rebar-brainstorm; ready to implement\n\nPurpose: dogfood a **self-contained, standard rebar MCP HTTP server** on the AWS box (Gerrit +\nreview-bot + opcert), exposing ALL rebar functionality, reachable by copilot/codex/claude. Setup\nmatches the user-facing docs; where docs are incomplete they are fixed (starling).\n\n### Settled decisions (all build-critical)\n1. **Exposure + auth** — nginx `/mcp/` TLS edge → loopback-bound `rebar-mcp` HTTP; verifier mode\n   `static`; per-client bearer PATs in `Authorization`. Research-confirmed all three clients support\n   static bearer; none require OAuth. This is the documented docs/mcp-auth.md §5 recipe, NOT the\n   opcert SigV4/proxy pattern.\n2. **Autodeploy drain** — **blue-green immutable-release**, modeled on the LOCAL `origin/main`-tracking\n   updater (sticky-genetic-narwhal: immutable release + atomic `current`-pointer swap +\n   retire-when-idle), NOT the review-bot stop-and-health-drain. Build new image → start new container\n   (one-in/one-out overlap cap + memory-pressure alarm; t4g.large 8 GiB, avoid forcing t4g.xlarge) →\n   health-check → atomically flip nginx `/mcp/` upstream → retire old off the critical path with\n   bounded retention + cap + SNS alert. `/health` `in_flight` counts only long-running/certified ops\n   and feeds the RETIRE check, not the deploy gate. No in-place reload (lazy-import hazard). Rationale:\n   eliminates review-bot bug 7b4a saturation/kill — a never-idle shared MCP server never blocks a\n   deploy or forces a kill; a killed op is client-visible + idempotent (event-sourced).\n3. **Certified-op routing** — register the box as a **trusted signing environment**\n   (.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml on main + verify.require_environment) so MCP-minted plan-review\n   + completion certs are enforceable (ADR 0049: exactly two op-cert kinds). **Code review = the\n   existing Gerrit LLM-Review vote, NOT a new op-cert.** opcert job-service + remote-cert coexist\n   (additive). The epic item-7 wording is corrected in guidance.\n\n### AWS cost note\nNo significant ongoing AWS-cost delta vs a single-container drain: both run one steady-state\ncontainer on the same t4g.large; blue-green's only lever is the transient 2× container RAM, capped\none-in/one-out + memory-pressure-alarmed so it never forces a larger instance. Retained images are\nbounded by existing docker prune (~pennies). The real recurring $ saving is off-AWS: blue-green\navoids the single-container pattern's wasted billable-LLM retries under saturation.\n\n### Decomposition (7 children; ADR blocks all)\n- deft-evolutive-mosasaur — ADR (exposure/auth + blue-green drain + certified-op routing) + ADR 0079\n  amendment. **Blocks all.**\n- cibophobic-holohedral-esok — infra: mcp compose svc + Dockerfile.mcp + nginx /mcp/ SWITCHABLE\n  upstream + /health in-flight gauge + SIGTERM grace. dep: mosasaur.\n- panicky-sylphish-foxterrier — autodeploy: mcp blue-green target (build→cutover→retire, retention/\n  cap/alert), independent multi-target, portable trigger. deps: mosasaur, esok.\n- exuberant-blockish-avians — secrets: SSM-materialized per-client bearer PATs (opcert-guard pattern,\n  not rsync — gotcha f600) + gitignored client-cred template + committed-secret guard. dep: mosasaur.\n- unmythical-uninspired-olm — client cfg: copilot/codex/claude static-bearer configs + basic read\n  smoke. deps: esok, avians.\n- inadequate-hydrated-starling — guidance/docs: AGENTS.md MCP-required policy (new-prohibition\n  consumer scan) + certified-op wording fix + docs/mcp-auth.md AWS recipe + client guide. deps:\n  mosasaur, spoiled-bionic-goose.\n- spoiled-bionic-goose (NEW) — trusted-env registration (enforceable MCP-minted op-certs). dep:\n  mosasaur. blocks starling.\n- creased-childlike-jackal — approval-gated live 3-client prod verification (human). dep: olm.\n\nPlan-review runs in dependency order: only mosasaur is unblocked now; the rest fast-fail\nINDETERMINATE until their blockers close and become claimable via `rebar ready`."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787598613584229001,"uuid":"444e6187-6f4e-4c7d-873d-fda45632186a"}